# Math

Use [Material math](https://squidfunk.github.io/mkdocs-material/reference/math/) for a formula that cannot be said in a sentence. `pymdownx.arithmatex` and KaTeX are enabled. Do not add MathJax.

These pages describe YAML fields. Write a simple ratio in words, as in "height divided by width", or put a token in backticks, as in `` `0.5` ``.

A display formula is a `$$` fence on its own lines, and an inline formula is `$f$` inside the sentence. Use one of those pairs. Do not mix in `\(` or `\[`.

```markdown
$$
\cos x=\sum_{k=0}^{\infty}\frac{(-1)^k}{(2k)!}x^{2k}
$$
```

- One formula per display block. Do not put prose inside the `$$` lines.
- KaTeX is the renderer. Do not add MathJax beside it.
